# Documentation Consolidation & Sync Strategy

This plan outlines how to move and organize all your research/brain files from the system-managed Gemini directory into your project, while maintaining their chronological and chat-based context.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Multi-Category Sorting**: Files are sorted into: Tasks, Planning, Learning, and Vision.
> 
> **Chronological Order**: 
> 1. **Folders**: Names are prefixed with `yyyy-MM-dd` (e.g., `2026-02-04_Auth-Setup`).
> 2. **Files**: Filenames are prefixed with `HH-mm` (e.g., `14-30_task.md`) to ensure they sort by time in your file explorer.

## Proposed Changes

We will create a consolidation script that does the following:
1. Loops through each "Session" folder in your Brain directory.
2. Identifies the primary task or topic of that session (by reading [task.md](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/ed5e0757-6cdd-4eaa-928b-7096a381c2a9/task.md)).
3. Copies all files (including [.resolved](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d7e3ed05-2fb9-4b12-97a8-302ab75b8083/task.md.resolved) and [task.md](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/ed5e0757-6cdd-4eaa-928b-7096a381c2a9/task.md)) into a structured folder in `apps/gurudevi-mobile/Docs v 3.0/brain_archive/`.

